    "lang": "en",
    "stem": "If you have a section of code that has one simple IF statement,  how many tests will be needed to achieve 100% branch  coverage?",
    "images": [],
    "options": [
      {
        "key": "a",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "b",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "c",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "d",
        "text": "Unknown with this information"
      }
    ],
    "correct": [
      "b"
    ],
    "multi": false,
    "explanation": "B is correct. A simple IF statement will be composed of If ... then ... else\t end if. There are two branch outcomes, one for the result of the If being  true and one for it being false. Since 100% branch coverage requires at  least one test case for each branch outcome, two tests are needed. A and C are incorrect because these are the wrong numbers of tests. D would be correct if this weren’t defined as a simple if statement  because a complex if statement could include more than two outcomes.",
    "knowledge_ref": "FL-4.3.2 (K2) Explain branch testing",
    "is_duplicate": false,
